  "staleRule": "Before sealing, a changed local generation prevents the request. At the server, a changed original remote head rejects the transaction. In either local-or-remote-head stale case neither work head advances, the client reclassifies, and the same reserved newWorkId/root is reused instead of creating another clone.",
  "newWorkCollisionRule": "If read-back proves that the reserved newWorkId is owned by a different operation, neither head has changed, and the response is newWorkAlreadyExists, the same pendingKeepBoth row retires that reservation and atomically reserves exactly one unused WorkID with its recomputed zero-parent root and a new operation ID. The local clone state is not duplicated; this collision path is not the stale-reuse path.",
  "atomicityRule": "The original Work remote-choice two-parent resolution, new Work zero-parent root, Conflict state, change events, and operation receipt commit in one server transaction."
